OL,3,ASwinney's emotional explanation for his
OL,4,Acommitment to independence
OL,5,
OL,6,FThis was a more emotional speech than
OL,7,Fwe are used to from John Swinney.
OL,9,FHis voice quivered as he explained that
OL,10,Fhis personal commitment to the cause is
OL,11,Ffor the future of his 15-year-old son,
OL,12,FMatthew.
OL,14,FThen the autocue stalled and the SNP
OL,15,Fleader is heard saying under his breath
OL,16,F"oh, come on".
OL,18,FA period of silence was broken by the
OL,19,Fconference crowd who came to his rescue
OL,20,Fwith a standing ovation.
